    <div class="bcolls bcolls--grouped">
<p class="blabel bcoll-group"><a href="/the-faith-received/all-works/?collection=all&amp;tradition=Protestant&amp;denomination=English+Divines">English Divines</a></p>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/all-works/?collection=all&amp;tradition=Protestant&amp;denomination=English+Divines&amp;party=Puritan">Puritan</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">2,936 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">The English Reformed line from Perkins to Owen, 1580&ndash;1700. Sermons, casuistry, controversy, practical divinity. Early English Books and our own editions, in the spelling they were printed in.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">William Perkins, Richard Sibbes, Richard Baxter, John Owen, Thomas Manton, Thomas Brooks, Jeremiah Burroughs, Joseph Caryl, Samuel Rutherford, John Bunyan</p>
      </article>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/all-works/?collection=all&amp;tradition=Protestant&amp;denomination=English+Divines&amp;party=Anglican">Anglican</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">1,687 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">The Church of England&rsquo;s divines from Jewel and Hooker to Tillotson. The case against Rome, the case against the Puritans, the sermons and the prayer book.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">Richard Hooker, Lancelot Andrewes, Joseph Hall, Jeremy Taylor, Henry Hammond, Simon Patrick, Edward Stillingfleet, John Tillotson, Gilbert Burnet, Richard Allestree</p>
      </article>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/all-works/?collection=all&amp;tradition=Protestant&amp;denomination=English+Divines&amp;party=Westminster+Assembly">Westminster Assembly</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">934 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">The divines who sat at Westminster, 1643&ndash;1653, and the Assembly&rsquo;s own minutes. Eighty-eight members are held here; their works also stand on the Puritan shelf.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">William Twisse, Stephen Marshall, Edmund Calamy, Thomas Goodwin, Edward Reynolds, Thomas Gataker, Jeremiah Burroughs, William Gouge, Samuel Rutherford, George Gillespie</p>
      </article>
<p class="tfr-browse-all"><a class="btrad-all" href="/the-faith-received/early-english-books/">All 15,569 Early English Books <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></p>
<p class="blabel bcoll-group">The Fathers</p>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/patrologia-latina/">Patrologia Latina</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">8,967 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">Migne&rsquo;s Latin fathers, Tertullian to Innocent III, in 217 volumes. For many of these works it is still the only edition.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">Augustine of Hippo, Jerome of Stridon, Ambrose of Milan, Gregory the Great, Bede the Venerable, Bernard of Clairvaux, Anselm of Canterbury, Peter Damian, Rabanus Maurus, Rupert of Deutz</p>
      </article>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/patrologia-graeca/">Patrologia Graeca</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">2,976 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">Migne&rsquo;s Greek fathers, the apostolic writers to the fall of Constantinople, Greek with the Latin facing.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">John Chrysostom, Origen, Athanasius, Basil the Great, Gregory of Nyssa, Gregory of Nazianzus, Eusebius of Caesarea, Cyril of Alexandria, John of Damascus, Theodoret of Cyrrhus</p>
      </article>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/patrologia-orientalis/">Eastern Fathers</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">400 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">The churches that wrote in Syriac, Coptic, Armenian, Arabic and Ge&#8217;ez, each text with a facing translation. Lives of the martyrs, liturgies, chronicles, theology.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">Severus of Antioch, Philoxenus of Mabbug, Jacob of Edessa, Aphrahat, Ephrem of Nisibis, Barhebraeus, Mark of Ephesus</p>
      </article>
<p class="blabel bcoll-group">Latin divinity, 1100&ndash;1750</p>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/latin-library/?tradition=Medieval">Medieval</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">357 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">The schoolmen: Sentences commentaries, summas, disputed questions, the canon law. Latin with English.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">Thomas Aquinas, Albert the Great, John Duns Scotus, Bonaventure, William of Ockham, Henry of Ghent, Johannes Capreolus, Denys the Carthusian, Gratian, Hostiensis</p>
      </article>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/latin-library/?tradition=Roman+Catholic">Roman Catholic</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">514 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">Trent and the schools after it: the Jesuits, the Dominicans, the Salamanca Carmelites, the manuals down to the twentieth century. Latin with English.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">Robert Bellarmine, Francisco Su&aacute;rez, Cornelius a Lapide, the Salamanticenses, John of St Thomas, Denis P&eacute;tau, Alfonso Salmer&oacute;n, Honor&eacute; Tournely, Caesar Baronius, the Council of Trent</p>
      </article>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/latin-library/?tradition=Reformed">Reformed</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">426 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">Calvin and the Reformed orthodox, 1536&ndash;1750: the systems, the disputations, the commentaries. Latin with English.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">John Calvin, Heinrich Bullinger, Theodore Beza, Girolamo Zanchi, Franciscus Junius, Amandus Polanus, Gisbertus Voetius, Johannes Cocceius, Francis Turretin, Johann Heinrich Heidegger</p>
      </article>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/latin-library/?tradition=Lutheran">Lutheran</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">280 works</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">Luther and the Lutheran dogmaticians, 1517&ndash;1750: the Concord line from Chemnitz to Calov and Quenstedt. Latin with English.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">Martin Luther, Philipp Melanchthon, Martin Chemnitz, Johann Gerhard, Abraham Calov, Johannes Andreas Quenstedt, Balthasar Meisner, Matthias Flacius Illyricus, Jesper Brochmand, Johann Franz Budde</p>
      </article>
<p class="blabel bcoll-group">The churches&rsquo; own words</p>
      <article class="bcoll">
        <h3 class="bcoll-name"><a href="/the-faith-received/confessions/">Creeds, Confessions &amp; Catechisms</a></h3>
        <p class="bcoll-n">260 documents</p>
        <p class="bcoll-what">What the churches said when asked to state what they believe, and the catechisms written to teach it. The Apostles&rsquo; Creed to the Savoy Declaration.</p>
        <p class="bcoll-who">The Ancient Creeds, Chalcedon, Trent, Augsburg, the First Helvetic, the Belgic, Heidelberg, the Thirty-nine Articles, Dort, the Formula of Concord, Westminster, the London Baptist Confession, Savoy</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
